content.text:
The root cause is the `recommendation` service, which crash-looped and never became available during the incident. Its effect reached users as HTTP 500s on the frontend `/recommendations` route.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "recommendation",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, attr_k8s_deployment_name, min(value) AS vmin, max(value) AS vmax, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric = 'k8s.deployment.available' AND service_name = 'recommendation' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "recommendation deployment reports zero available replicas for the entire abnormal window, versus one in normal."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT time, value FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric = 'k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'recommendation%' ORDER BY time", "claim": "recommendation pod restart count climbs from 2 to 6 during the abnormal window; normal period shows 0."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'recommendation' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "recommendation emits no spans in the abnormal window, although it had 789 spans in the normal period."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "recommendation",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE attr_status_code = 'Error' GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY n DESC", "claim": "All 310 errors are frontend's recommendation gRPC calls and HTTP /recommendations 500s, the only error spans in the window."}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

